    C("guides/cloud-vs-on-premise-hospital-software", "Cloud vs On-Premise Hospital Software: Which Is Right? | QueroCura",
      "Cloud or on-premise hospital management software? A fair comparison of cost, security, uptime, data location and AI for hospitals in India.",
      "Cloud vs on-premise", "Cloud vs on-premise hospital software: which is right for you?",
      "Cloud software runs on the vendor's servers and is used through a browser; on-premise software runs on servers inside the hospital. Neither is always better. Here is a fair comparison for Indian hospitals, and a common middle path.",
      [{"h2": "Side by side", "table": {"head": ["", "Cloud", "On-premise"], "rows": [
           ["Upfront cost", "Low: no servers to buy", "High: servers, backup, licences"], ["Running cost", "Subscription", "IT staff, power, upgrades"],
           ["Setup time", "Days", "Weeks to months"], ["Updates", "Automatic", "Planned by your IT team"], ["Internet outage", "Needs a backup connection", "Keeps working inside the hospital"],
           ["Data location", "Vendor's data centre", "Inside your building"], ["Security", "Vendor's specialists; check their controls", "Your team's responsibility"]]}},
       {"h2": "The middle path", "p": ["Many hospitals run day-to-day operations in the cloud and keep the most sensitive or heaviest workloads on site. For example, QueroCura's hospital management system works through a browser, while its AI imaging engine can run on the hospital's own server so scans never leave the building."]},
       {"h2": "Questions to ask any vendor", "ul": ["Where is our data stored, and who can access it?", "What happens during an internet outage?", "How are backups made and tested?", "Can we export all our data if we leave?", "Is every access logged?"]}],
      [["Is cloud hospital software safe?", "It can be, if the vendor encrypts data, controls and logs access, backs up reliably and meets Indian data-protection law. Ask for specifics."]],
      kind="guide", related=["ai-medical-imaging", "guides/how-to-choose-a-hospital-management-system", "hospital-management-system"]),
    C("guides/hospital-management-system-implementation-plan", "HMS Implementation Plan: Go Live in 30 Days | QueroCura",
      "A practical 30-day plan for implementing a hospital management system: setup, data, training, a pilot and go-live, with the mistakes to avoid.",
      "HMS implementation", "How to implement a hospital management system: a 30-day plan",
      "Most HMS projects fail not because of the software but because of the rollout: too much at once, too little training, no pilot. This plan takes a small or mid-sized hospital from signing to go-live in about 30 days.",
      [{"h2": "Week 1: set up", "ul": ["Agree three goals (for example, shorter OPD waits, no unbilled services, a live bed board).", "Create departments, wards, beds, theatres and the price list.", "Create roles and invite staff with two-step sign-in."]},
       {"h2": "Week 2: data and training", "ul": ["Load doctors' schedules and current in-patients.", "Train each role on its own screens only, in short sessions.", "Name one champion per department."]},
       {"h2": "Week 3: pilot", "ul": ["Run one OPD and the billing desk on the new system for a week.", "Fix friction daily; measure waiting time and unbilled services."]},
       {"h2": "Week 4: go live", "ul": ["Switch the remaining departments over in a planned order.", "Keep champions on the floor for the first days.", "Review the three goals at the end of the month."]},
       {"h2": "Mistakes to avoid", "ul": ["Going live everywhere on the same day.", "Training everyone on everything.", "Leaving the price list until the last day.", "No owner for each department's problems."]}],
      [["How long does it take to implement a hospital management system?", "From a few weeks for clinics and small hospitals to several months for large ones. With a ready setup plan, a small hospital can go live in about 30 days."]],
      kind="guide", related=["guides/hospital-management-system-features", "nursing-home-software", "hospital-management-system"]),
